Ending_02
[background fade="0.0"]
Marloch: I am done taking. For once  just once  I would like to give something back, without asking anything in return.
catherine: Marloch, don't
Marloch: My immortality, for your ordinary, breakable, wonderful life. It's not a trade. It's a gift. Take it.
Narrator: Before she can refuse again, it's already done. Marloch's form flickers  ancient, then young, then achingly human, white-haired, mortal  and then still.
catherine: You didn't have to.
Narrator: She leaves Shateroo the next morning, alive, human, and carrying a debt she will spend the rest of her life trying to be worthy of.
[signal arg="game_end"]